steps.text:
`.then` on a settled promise queues its reaction at once. On a pending promise it only registers it; the job is queued when the promise settles [[c:reaction-on-settle]]. Order follows queueing time, not the line where `.then` was written.

Each `.then` returns a new promise, settled only when its handler has run, so a chain moves one hop per microtask and two chains interleave:
```js
const a = Promise.resolve();
a.then(() => log('a1')).then(() => log('a2'));
a.then(() => log('b1')).then(() => log('b2'));
// a1 b1 a2 b2
```
`queueMicrotask(fn)` joins the same queue with no promise around it. One difference: an error thrown in it is reported as a normal exception, not as a rejected promise [[c:queuemicrotask-errors]].

variants.stem:
What does this log?
```js
const log = console.log;
setTimeout(() => log('t'));
Promise.resolve().then(() => log('p1'))
  .then(() => log('p2'));
queueMicrotask(() => log('q'));
log('s');
```

What does this log?
```js
const log = console.log;
setTimeout(() => log('t'));
queueMicrotask(() => {
  log('m1');
  queueMicrotask(() => log('m3'));
});
queueMicrotask(() => log('m2'));
```

What does this log?
```js
const log = console.log;
let res;
const p = new Promise((r) => (res = r));
p.then(() => log('p'));
Promise.resolve().then(() => log('a'))
  .then(() => log('b'));
res();
log('s');
```

What does this log?
```js
const log = console.log;
const p = new Promise((r) => {
  log('e');
  r();
});
queueMicrotask(() => log('q'));
p.then(() => log('p'));
log('s');
```

What does this log?
```js
const log = console.log;
setTimeout(() => {
  log('t1');
  Promise.resolve().then(() => log('p'));
});
setTimeout(() => log('t2'));
```

What does this log?
```js
const log = console.log;
setTimeout(() => log('t1'));
setTimeout(() => {
  log('t2');
  queueMicrotask(() => log('m'));
});
setTimeout(() => log('t3'));
```

What does this log?
```js
const log = console.log;
let n = 0;
setTimeout(() => log('timer'));
function spin() {
  log('m' + n);
  if (++n < 3) queueMicrotask(spin);
}
queueMicrotask(spin);
```

This waits for a flag that a `setTimeout` callback sets 100 ms later. What happens?
```js
async function waitReady() {
  while (!ready) await null;
  start();
}
```

In a browser, the user clicks `btn`. What is logged?
```js
const log = console.log;
btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
  Promise.resolve().then(() => log('p1'));
  log('L1');
});
btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
  Promise.resolve().then(() => log('p2'));
  log('L2');
});
```

In a browser, a script runs this. What is logged?
```js
const log = console.log;
btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
  Promise.resolve().then(() => log('p1'));
  log('L1');
});
btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
  Promise.resolve().then(() => log('p2'));
  log('L2');
});
btn.click();
log('after');
```

In Node, what does this log?
```js
const log = console.log;
const t = new EventTarget();
t.addEventListener('go', () => {
  Promise.resolve().then(() => log('p1'));
  log('L1');
});
t.addEventListener('go', () => {
  Promise.resolve().then(() => log('p2'));
  log('L2');
});
t.dispatchEvent(new Event('go'));
log('after');
```
